# Code Style

Follow existing TypeScript patterns before adding abstractions.

Use canonical values from `frontend/src/shared/constants/lumina.ts` and `backend/src/contracts/lumina.ts`: `encryptedHuggingFaceToken`, `huggingFaceTokenConfigured`, `browser`, `cloud_ai`, `restore_face`, `text_overlay`.

Frontend API clients should throw typed API errors. Backend errors must use user-safe messages and must not expose secrets, tokens, stack traces, or provider response bodies.

Keep edits small and scoped. Do not move modules or rewrite architecture unless the task requires it.
